<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27988" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mărăthos</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-us</span></b> , i, f.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μάραθος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an ancient Phœnician city,
				opposite the island of Arados</i>, near the modern <i>Ainel-Hye</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 12,
				3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 20, 17, § 78</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Curt. 4, 1,
				6</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mărăthēnus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>from
				Marathos, Marathene</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Menelaüs,</span>”
				<i>a rhetorician from Marathos</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Brut. 26, 100</span></i>
			 Meyer.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
